{"step_index":1468,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-05-15T20:46:50Z","content":"I owe you an apology. I figured out why you were seeing nothing. \n\nThe data **was** arriving successfully from Autodesk (I could see 1 Hub and 63 Projects in the logs), but I had a typo in the Dashboard code. The dropdown was looking for a field called `name`, but Autodesk sends it as `attributes.name`. Because of this, it was literally rendering \"invisible\" text options in the dropdown. It looked empty, but the data was there.\n\nI have fixed the dropdowns so they can actually read the names, and I also spotted that the Excel file endpoint was missing from my consolidation, so I added that back too.\n\n**Could you refresh http://localhost:5173 one more time?** The visible text is back. This shouldn't take any more debugging, you should be straight back to where you were with your ACC sync."}
