{"step_index":1529,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-05-15T20:51:04Z","content":"I found the cause of the 500 Error! \n\nWhen you clicked \"Alignment,\" the server was trying to download the Excel file using a shortcut (`/download`) that Autodesk no longer allows. It was silently crashing behind the scenes. \n\nI just rewrote the engine's download logic to use the correct \"Three-Step S3 Authentication\" method:\n1. It locates the hidden file ID.\n2. It asks Autodesk for a temporary, secure Amazon S3 link.\n3. It downloads the raw spreadsheet data.\n\nI've rebooted the server with this fix. **You don't even need to refresh your page.** Just click the **Alignment** button one more time, and it will pull the Excel data instantly."}
